    "stale_revision_and_concurrent_edits": {
      "description": "Every planning mutation quotes the revision the screen was SHOWN. A second editor working from the revision the first one replaced is refused with the current number (23514) rather than applied on top of somebody else's edit. An order that LEAVES OUT one of the day's jobs is refused too: a screen built from a stale read would otherwise silently drop the stop it had not seen, and the drop would look like a decision. Retries are per operation: the same key with the same intent returns the stored receipt with `replayed: true` and creates no second revision; the same key with a DIFFERENT order is 23505.",
      "accepted": {
        "stops": [
          {
            "job_id": "job-9",
            "position": 1,
            "order_state": "explicit"
          },
          {
            "job_id": "job-10",
