    "blocked_broken_and_finished_are_not_completed": {
      "description": "FIVE states that must never collapse into one another: cancelled (commercial, on the job), skipped (the owner's), blocked (the crew went and could not get in), work_finished (the crew downed tools) and accepted_completed (the SERVER accepted a completion with its evidence, Batch 11.1). A report never changes the job's status and never completes or cancels anything, and the receipts say so in `job_status_changed` and `completion_recorded`. A blocked-access report blocks the stop, because that is what the crew is saying; a breakdown does not, because a broken washer does not necessarily stop the visit. Resolving is the owner's, reasoned, and recorded once. 11.1's gate is still the only way to complete: a direct status='completed' is refused.",
