    "notification_outcomes": {
      "description": "Two deliberate crew actions through the EXISTING notifications table. Nothing sends on opening a screen, changing a route or reading a location: there is no trigger and no scheduler. FIVE outcomes, four of which are not a successful send -- `accepted` (recorded and queued), `delivered`, `provider_failed`, `unknown` (we asked and do not know, which is NOT success) and `unavailable` (no provider configured, or no number on file: two different reasons fixed by different people). The recipient is resolved from the JOB's customer and is never read back -- the reads report `recipient_known` instead. One live request per job per kind, so two \"on the way\" texts for one visit is a conflict. THE HONEST RETRY RULE: `unknown` stays live and keeps blocking a second request, because the provider may have neither idempotency nor an outcome lookup and a retry might be the customer's second identical text; clearing it is a human decision. A `provider_failed` request no longer blocks a deliberate retry. No message payload ever carries an access code.",
